# Cusimanse Goose project guidance

- Treat the Markdown contract as the research scope and safety statement.
- Treat the selected Goose recipe as the executable workflow definition.
- Use Goose Plan/Todo for task decomposition.
- Prefer Skills for reusable security-research instructions.
- Use Summon/subrecipes for bounded specialist work and parallel work only when outputs do not conflict.
- Prefer Container Use when the workload needs an isolated environment.
- Never treat model output as evidence; cite observable files and command output.
- Do not access unrelated credentials, host data or repositories.
- Keep research artifacts under the experiment run directory.
